Intended use: research only. Nothing radiarch produces is for clinical
use. Every result carries that statement (see README.md, "Intended use").

This product includes or runs software developed by others:

- OpenTPS core, https://gitlab.com/openmcsquare/opentps, Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright UCLouvain. Parts of radiarch are ports of it: the contour
  rasterizer (services/contour_raster.py), the CT calibration and material
  database reader (services/proton_rsp.py), the spot placement
  (services/spot_placement.py), the MCsquare file protocol
  (services/dose_engines/mcsquare_driver.py, the configuration template
  services/dose_engines/mcsquare_config_template.txt) and the CCC file
  protocol (services/dose_engines/ccc_driver.py). Nothing of OpenTPS is
  imported or shipped as code.

- MCsquare, https://gitlab.com/openmcsquare/MCsquare, Apache License 2.0.
  The launcher, Linux binaries, material tables, beam data libraries and
  scanner calibration tables are shipped under engines/mcsquare/ (the copy
  packaged by OpenTPS core, whose licence is engines/mcsquare/LICENSE-OpenTPS)
  and are run as separate processes.

- WiscPlan collapsed-cone photon dose engine (CCC_DoseEngine), GNU General
  Public License version 2, shipped as source and a prebuilt Linux binary
  under engines/ccc/ (licence: engines/ccc/licenseWiscPlan.txt). radiarch
  runs it only as a separate program that exchanges files with it; nothing in
  radiarch links to or imports it.

- Test data: the SimpleFantomWithStruct DICOM set from the OpenTPS test data,
  under tests/data/.
